          "open_questions": [
            "Network (wave 3): STILL UNRESOLVED; card_product.network left null, one Visa candidate kept as a hint only. The CS page carries the \"Visa Exclusive Offers\" block and no RuPay block, and the card image asset is named \"CS_Credit_Card Op3_without-VISA\" (a Visa logo was edited out of that art file), which points to Visa, but the offers block is template text shared across AU pages and a file name is not a network mark. The card art as displayed (list tile and product page) shows no network mark. Routes tried on 2026-11-07, none states the network: card front art on the AU credit card list tile and on the product page (images opened and read, no network mark on the front); the product page text and popups; AU KFS v1.9, MITC v2.23 and Cardmember Agreement (only the generic \"VISA/RuPay\"); the AU domestic lounge, Priority Pass and railway lounge T&Cs (\"Visa/RuPay\" generic, so the lounge programme covers Visa and RuPay cards only); the card liability insurance and welcome-benefit T&Cs; AU press releases and blogs; the AU offers site (card-level offers need a login); visa.co.in card-finder and offers pages (generic, no AU card named); npci.org.in RuPay pages (no issuer or card list); rupay.co.in offers (bot-protected, not opened). The \"Visa Exclusive Offers\" block is template text shared across AU pages (it also sits on the RuPay-only Kosmo page) and was not used. Needs a person: ask AU, or read the card back or a statement.",
            "Value of one AU Reward Point: not stated for this card (CS reward T&C, welcome and ICSI T&Cs, KFS, MITC, CMA and the Rewardz FAQ read; the FAQ says it depends on card variant and redemption category). Left null on purpose. AU's 2 Jun 2023 notice gives Rs 0.20 per point only for gift card/voucher redemption on all variants; not used as a card value.",
